Note: The above solution uses a recursive depth-first search (DFS) algorithm to find the path from the start to the goal. It keeps track of the current path and backtracks when it reaches a dead end. If the start and goal are the same and the start is free, it immediately returns a list containing the start. If the start or goal is a wall, or no path exists, it returns an empty list.

